    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "First Clas\nWine List",
      "White\nWine\nhite\nWine\n1997\n1991\nGRAND VIN DE BOURGOGNE\nDOMAINE DE LA BARONN\nPOUILLY-FUISSE\nAppellaties Poilty-Fainst Controlse\nPOUILLY-FUISSE 1997\nGreatly influenced by the distinctive soil type, mineral and\nplant-based aromas, as well as walnut and grilled almonds\ncomplimented by a floral touch with a hint of honey. Rich\nand generous, with mineral undertones confirming the\norigins of this distinctive Pouilly - Fuisse. Although Pouilly -\nFuisse is often prefered young to better appreciate is\ndistinctive aromas.\nAmerican\nWinemerican\nWine\nRED WINE\nChatan Her lichelle\nCOLUMBIA VALLEY\nMERLOT\nMERLOT 1996\nCHATEAU STE MICHELLE\nPure red fruit aromas cherry and raspberry introduce this\nwine, accented with vanilla and sweet cider. A find balance\nof oak and fruit emerges on the palate. Rich and supple,\nwith flavors of ripe raspberry, cherry cider and smooth oak,\nthis Merlot is delightfully soft.\nWHITE WINE\nChakan Nichelle\n10OG\nINDIAN WELLS VINEYARD\nCHARDONNA\nColumbia Vall\nCHARDONNAY 1998,\nINDIAN WELLS WINEYARD,\nCHATEAU STE MICHELLE\nMike januik crafted the 1998 vintage to showcase the\ndistinctive aromas and flavos of this vineyard. The wine was\nsur lie aged for 10 months after fermentation in 100%\nFrench oak barrel.\nA balanced wine with classic apple and spice notes and\ncitrus flavors. The viscous, silky mouthfeel is enhanced by a\nlong and generous finish."
    ],
